## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/h24/ee.png" alt="Estonia" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', marginRight: '8px'}} />Estonia

Estonia is a digitally advanced Baltic microstate whose entire strategic orientation constitutes a continuous response to the existential problem of surviving beside Russia without sufficient mass to defend itself alone. This week demonstrated the stress-testing of Estonia's alliance architecture: when faced with US pressure over Greenland, Estonia chose EU solidarity and alliance principles over avoiding displeasure from its most critical security guarantor. The country's response—participating in EU emergency meetings while maintaining military cooperation commitments despite economic threats—reveals both the depth of institutional embedding and the priority placed on alliance cohesion over bilateral accommodation. Estonia continues spending 5% of GDP on defense while achieving the world's highest density of unicorn companies and ranking 2nd globally in press freedom, but its willingness to risk US displeasure for alliance solidarity represents a notable evolution in how it manages competing alliance pressures.

**Key developments:**

- **Diplomatic:** Foreign Minister Tsahkna participated in emergency EU meetings in Brussels regarding Trump's Greenland threats, emphasizing European unity behind Denmark. PM Michal also attended emergency European Council meeting to discuss transatlantic developments. *([postimees.ee](https://postimees.ee/8399050/valisminister-tsahkna-trump-peab-saama-sonumi-et-euroopa-on-uhtne-taani-ja-groonimaa-selja-taga-see-on-eluliselt-tahtis), 2026-01-18)*
- **Security:** Defense Minister Pevkur confirmed Estonia will proceed with planned participation in Denmark's Arctic Endurance military drill despite Trump's threat of higher tariffs on countries sending troops, stating there's no need to link economic matters to military exercises. *([news.err.ee](https://news.err.ee/1609914256/defense-minister-estonia-still-planning-to-take-part-in-danish-drills-in-greenland), 2026-01-18)*
- **Security:** Defense Minister Pevkur and other officials expressed skepticism about EU defense capabilities independent of NATO, emphasizing that military planning and operations must remain within NATO frameworks rather than duplicating structures through concepts like a 100,000-person European unit. *([err.ee](https://www.err.ee/1609913809/nato-le-lootvad-eesti-poliitikud-euroopa-iseseisvasse-kaitsesse-ei-usu), 2026-01-18)*
- **Economic:** Madis Müller was not selected for the European Central Bank vice president role, with eurozone finance ministers choosing Croatian candidate Boris Vujcic instead. Müller's term as Bank of Estonia president ends in June 2026. *([err.ee](https://err.ee/1609915528/madis-mullerist-ei-saa-euroopa-keskpanga-asepresidenti), 2026-01-19)*
- **Institutional:** Bank of Estonia president Madis Müller was not selected for ECB vice president position, representing a missed opportunity for Estonian influence in eurozone monetary policy leadership. *([err.ee](https://err.ee/1609915528/madis-mullerist-ei-saa-euroopa-keskpanga-asepresidenti), 2026-01-19)*

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **Tsahkna conducts extensive international diplomatic outreach** — Foreign Minister Tsahkna engaged in multiple diplomatic activities including meeting with Belarusian opposition leader Tsikhanouskaya, making statements on Iran human rights, Ukraine support, EU-Russia policy failures, and Russian shadow fleet threats. *([hibya.com](https://tsikhanouskaya.org/en/news/sviatlana-tsikhanouskaya-met-with-estonias-minister-of-foreign-affairs-margus-tsahkna-2.html))*
- **Coop Pank faces client complaints over money transfers and announces expansion strategy** — Estonian bank Coop Pank experienced customer complaints about delayed money transfers and funds being held for compliance checks. The bank separately announced strategic plans to double profits by 2030 and expand market share against larger competitors. *([elu24.postimees.ee](https://elu24.postimees.ee/8400060/isikliku-raha-kinnihoid-coop-pangas-tekitab-klientides-muret-ootasin-oma-raha-kaks-nadalat))*
- **Estonian Defense League recognizes annual best members in ceremony** — Kaitseliit held its 16th annual awards ceremony in Tallinn recognizing the best defense league member, women's home defense member, and youth leaders for 2026. *([lounaeestlane.ee](https://lounaeestlane.ee/kaitseliit-tunnustas-oma-parimaid-liikmeid/))*
- **Bank of Estonia releases commemorative coin for Milano-Cortina Olympics** — Estonian central bank issued a silver commemorative coin dedicated to Estonian athletes participating in the 2026 Winter Olympics in Milano and Cortina d'Ampezzo. *([postimees.ee](https://www.postimees.ee/8402436/fotod-eesti-pank-esitles-milano-cortina-omile-puhendatud-meenemunti))*
</Accordion>


